Before any Git-related task, read and follow:

@agent/rules/git-and-branches.md

Also consult these when relevant:

@agent/workflows/feature-development.md
@agent/templates/handoff.md
@agent/specs/ci-and-quality-gates.md

`26455900-CS345/` is the only Git repository. Run Git from that directory or
with `git -C 26455900-CS345`. The default branch is `main`, the remote is
`origin`, and the ordinary authorised write path is add, commit, then
`git push origin main`.

Do not run Git at the workspace root. Do not create feature, submission, or
publication branches, pull requests, merge requests, export commits, or
synchronisation workflows unless explicitly asked. Git writes still require a
human request under @agent/rules/git-and-branches.md.
